NOTICE: OpenBSD-derived files

Files under sys/ that are ports of OpenBSD sources carry their original
copyright notice and license at the top of the file, between the
<LICENSES> and </LICENSES> markers. That license governs that file. The
licenses accepted for ported files are ISC, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause,
BSD-4-Clause (its advertising clause included), MIT, the Carnegie Mellon
(Mach) license, Poul-Henning Kamp's beerware license, John S. Dyson's
license (sys_pipe.c, pipe.h), the zlib license (sys/lib/libz) and the
IPsec notice of Ioannidis, Keromytis, Provos and Hallqvist (sys/netinet and
sys/crypto), Carnegie Mellon's ALTQ notice and M.I.T.'s notice (sys/net), the
notice of Julian Elischer / TRW Financial Systems (sys/scsi); files
in the public domain keep their public-domain notice. Provenance
per file is recorded in ports.toml; the upstream commit is recorded in
reference/PINNED.md. The names of OpenBSD contributors may not be used to
endorse or promote this project without their written permission
(BSD-3-Clause, clause 3).

Files ported from zlib (Copyright (C) 1995-2026 Jean-loup Gailly and Mark
Adler) are altered source versions: they are rewritten in Rust and are not
the original software (zlib license, clause 2). Their license text is kept
in full in each file.
